<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept rubber exports up.</title>
<headline>Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept rubber exports up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's rubber exports rose 14.2 percent to $35.3 million in the first nine months of 1996 from $30.9 million each in the same period in 1995 and 1994.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry released the data ahead of President Suharto's unveiling of the 1997/98 (April-March) state budget in parliament on Monday.</p>
<p>Indonesia is the world's largest rubber producer after Thailand.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
